// Session VWAP reclaim. Price trades below the anchored session VWAP, then
// reclaims it and holds. VWAP_RECLAIM_HOLD_BARS is the number of consecutive
// closed 5m bars that have closed above session VWAP since the most recent close
// below it; the host publishes 0 when no close below VWAP has occurred this
// session. VWAP_DIP_DEPTH_PCT is how far below session VWAP the lowest close of
// that dip reached, as a positive percentage of VWAP.
// REGIME: an intraday session that sold off into value and is being bought
// back. Do NOT fire in chop that oscillates across VWAP every few bars - the
// hold count and the depth term are both there to reject it.
// CONDITIONS: three consecutive closes above session VWAP (fifteen minutes of
// holding, not a wick through the level) after a dip that reached at least
// 0.3 percent below it.
// INVALIDATION: a close back below session VWAP, which resets the hold count to
// zero and ends the proposal.
// SHAPE: 5m; a flush below value, a reclaim, and three bars of acceptance above
// it.
// NOT vwap_band_reversion: that uses a rolling twenty-bar VWAP with no session
// anchor and buys into a narrowing discount while price is still below it.
// This one uses an anchored session VWAP and waits for price to reclaim and
// hold above it before proposing anything.
// CALIBRATED ON: US equity index ETF, regular session, 5m bars. The VWAP is
// anchored at the regular-session open and resets every session; anchored,
// session and rolling VWAP are three different levels and the rule cannot tell
// them apart, so the host must publish exactly this one. The 0.3 percent depth
// is absolute and does not travel to instruments with a different intraday
// range.
strategy VwapReclaim {

    every 5m {

        if VWAP_RECLAIM_HOLD_BARS >= 3 and VWAP_DIP_DEPTH_PCT >= 0.3 {

            buy(SPY, 0.6)

        }

    }

}
